 "postHocFindings (post hoc, not part of the rule)": [
  "post hoc: the confirmatory slice does not confirm round 7. Pool: truncated = truncated-guard (no fallback fired) 0.632 vs keywordNarrow 0.633, interval [-0.101, +0.077], vs keywordBroad [-0.008, +0.179]; it still beats frozen (0.472) by a wide margin, as on poolA/poolB. Window: truncated 0.484, guard 0.517, frozen 0.583, all far below keywordNarrow 0.682.",
  "post hoc: fresh-3's teaching window is thin. earnings and courts got ONE relevant answer each (of 5-10 shown); with one taught score the relevant sd hits the 0.05 floor and pi its 1/n bound, so all three designs accept 2-3 articles (earnings 0.170 vs keyword 0.873, courts 0.333 vs 0.889). These two profiles alone cost about 0.14 of macro T11F in the window protocol, identically for all candidates.",
  "post hoc: the guard did what it was for: robotics window N=5 truncated ended at mu1 <= mu0 (mu1 -0.08, pi 0.5), the Platt fallback accepted 1,385 of 1,388 (T11F 0.02, Brier skill -1.05 for the profile); the round-2 EM fallback gave robotics 0.425. It was the only fallback in a scored unit in either protocol.",
  "post hoc: where the truncated fit does converge well apart, it is often too far below the frozen fit in the window: chips N=5 accepted 7 (0.29) vs frozen 22 (0.68), robotics N=10 4 vs 20. With few window answers the truncation term pulls the relevant component down to sd ~0.3 and pi to its lower bound.",
  "post hoc: in the pool protocol the truncated fit fixes the frozen design's starvation (funding 0.023 -> 0.910, chips 0.285 -> 0.629, coding 0.440 -> 0.762) but courts (0.513 vs keyword 0.895, pi at 1/n, s1 0.15) and regulation (0.253 vs 0.314) stay below the keyword, and safety/open-models get the opposite failure (mu1 near 1, pi 0.05-0.19, 26-59 accepted).",
  "post hoc: many fits in all candidates end with pi at its lower bound 1/n; the plug-in threshold then accepts only the few top articles. This bound-hitting, not the mu1 <= mu0 mode, is the dominant failure on fresh-3.",
  "post hoc: no-relevant-answer keyword fallbacks: window 4 units (biology, energy; all unscored); pool none."
 ],
 "noneEligible": "No change to the package; the exam stays sealed. Why: on unseen data, truncated's pool interval vs keywordNarrow is [-0.101, +0.077] (bar -0.05) and vs keywordBroad [-0.008, +0.179] (bar 0); in the window protocol every candidate's lower bound vs keywordNarrow is below -0.30 and none beats keywordBroad. The round-7 pool result did not replicate on fresh-3."
